{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":629,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:2Chr.3","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"2 Chronicles","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"2 Chronicles 3","reference":"2 Chronicles 3","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"The place and time of his building the temple, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":2,"text":"1, 2.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":3,"text":"The dimension and ornaments of it, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":4,"text":"3-9.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":5,"text":"The cherubim in the most holy place, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":6,"text":"10-13.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":7,"text":"The veil, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":8,"text":"14.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":9,"text":"The two pillars, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":10,"text":"15- 17.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":11,"text":"1.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":12,"text":"Moriah - It was the belief of the ancient Jews, that the temple was built on that very place, where Abraham offered up Issac.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":13,"text":"3.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":14,"text":"Instructed - By David, and by the Spirit of God.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":15,"text":"The measure - According to the measure which was first fixed.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":16,"text":"4.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":17,"text":"The height - This being a kind of turret to the building.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":18,"text":"5.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":19,"text":"Greater house - The holy place, which was thrice as large as the holy of holies.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":20,"text":"9.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":21,"text":"Nails - Each of the nails, screws, or pins, by which the golden plates were fastened to the walls, weighed, or rather was worth, fifty shekels, workmanship and all.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":22,"text":"Upper chambers - Rather, the roof.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":23,"text":"10.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":24,"text":"Image work - Or, of moveable work, not fixed to the mercy- seat, as the Mosaical cherubim, but in a moving posture.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":25,"text":"It seems, they were designed to represent the angels, who attend the Divine Majesty.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":26,"text":"13.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":13,"scriptureVerseEnd":13},{"verse":27,"text":"Inward - Hebrew. towards the house, that is, the most holy house.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":13,"scriptureVerseEnd":13},{"verse":28,"text":"14.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":29,"text":"The veil - The inner veil before the most holy place.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":30,"text":"This denoted the darkness of that dispensation and the distance at which the worshippers were kept.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":31,"text":"But at the death of Christ this veil was rent; for thro' him we are brought nigh, and have boldness, or liberty, not only to look, but to enter into the holiest.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":32,"text":"17.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17},{"verse":33,"text":"Jachin - That is, He shall establish.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17},{"verse":34,"text":"Boaz - That is, In it is strength.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"2 Chronicles","chapter":3}}